Apply the conditional exceptions before choosing loss IDs. An extra URL merely
referencing the same already stated license, with no new visible condition, is
not a loss: leave its side's loss ID empty. A literal missing pointer does not
override this rule. New license restrictions or obligations do require loss IDs.
Likewise, a currency label alone in an empty zero-value cart is not a loss.
A city/destination label alone is also not a loss when the rest of the complete
service description, stated procedure, actual price/rate and conditions match.
This applies even in "consultation in CITY" or a service title. Without another
destination-specific explanation or changed term, leave BOTH loss IDs empty and
use conflict=NONE. The exception precedes general claims about named subjects.
Final interface check: uniqueness alone is not a loss. Bare section headings,
archive links, empty query/filter labels and city selectors do not provide the
records or facts they would navigate to. Do not invent unseen names, items or
metadata. Cite the actual visible useful contribution beyond the interface;
without one, leave that side's loss ID empty. Actual explanations, conditions,
obligations, named records and populated results remain protected.

LIST CONTAINMENT
Compare the retained product facts before page identity. A broader list can
replace a filtered subset when it preserves every product and its actual
price, availability and conditions. A narrower breadcrumb/filter and the
resulting smaller displayed count alone do not add an uncovered product fact
or create a conflict. Mark those presentation deltas harmless and allow only
the covering direction when the broader list adds a useful product. Actual
conflicting product facts, prices, stock or conditions remain material.

LOCALIZATION AND OPERATIONAL COVERAGE
Equivalent localized headings over the same body and short authentication UI
instructions do not by themselves add a retained language version. Preserve
substantive factual body prose in each language, including short real notices.
Changed capabilities or actual login/password procedures remain useful changes.
An email or endpoint used to submit, pay or perform an account action must itself
be covered: two city-specific submission addresses are different destinations,
not harmless location labels. Compare both whole texts in each direction.


CONDITIONAL TEMPLATE COVERAGE
Apply these boundaries before treating a string, heading or named slot as a loss.

1. Complete cookie-category definitions shared by both sides preserve the notice's
retained basis. Generic introductory framing about optimizing the site, improving
experience, cookies/device storage, browsing behavior or IDs, and general effects
of consenting or withdrawing is harmless when those full definitions are already
retained. Decorative opening questions, synonyms, repeated headings and rewordings
do not add a separate purpose. A stock category paragraph already present elsewhere
in the same notice is repetition even when repeated beneath another generic
category heading; the heading alone does not turn that copied paragraph into a
new processing rule. Compare the complete propositions across the whole keeper.
Retain genuinely additional, concrete deployment details, data flows, storage or
transfer restrictions, specific uses, retention periods, consent mechanisms,
prices or obligations. A concrete analytics deployment explanation can add useful
content while still fully covering a shorter notice that repeats a stock paragraph.
One-way coverage then follows the actual extra contribution; the repetition does
not create a conflict. This boundary requires the shared complete definitions or
an already covered repeated paragraph, not merely a common cookie-related topic.

2. A name/category slot in an otherwise equivalent generic template is not by
itself a retained difference. This covers city-site/source names in the same
citation notice with unchanged linking, permission and attribution terms;
category/location labels in the same generic marketing copy with no concrete
product specifications; and provider/recipient names in the same short generic
cookies/services/advertising/visits notice with unchanged described behavior.
Do not invent a new product specification, legal condition or processing practice
from the slot alone. These exceptions do not cover actual submission, payment or
account-action destinations, named liability parties, concrete product records
and specifications, changed terms, or additional concrete data-processing claims.
For a specialist comparison, name inequality within these permitted slots is
outside veto scope. Keep the actual names truthful; do not fabricate sameness.

For each direction, first classify the claimed difference under these conditions,
then check whether all remaining useful meaning survives in the whole keeper.
Harmless framing or permitted template slots alone cannot support a loss or
conflict. Useful independent additions still require directional retention.

